                <pb facs="0324" n="244" sameAs="frus:frus1930v01/pg244"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">560.M5/150: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in
                        Switzerland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Wilson</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-10-14T14:00:00-05:00">October 14, 1930—2
                        p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>98. Legation’s telegram 96, October 9, 10 a.m.<anchor n="53" xml:id="d229-f1"/>
                    Express to Secretary General appreciation of offer of facilities and advise him
                    that American Consul at Geneva will be instructed to follow the proceedings.
                    Inform Gilbert.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
